articles.content_en:
Article 10 Upon examination by the court, the defendant's pre-trial confession may be read out and cross-examined in court under any of the following circumstances:
(1) The defendant or his defense counsel has not provided relevant leads or evidence regarding illegal evidence collection;
(2) The defendant or his defense counsel has provided relevant leads or evidence regarding illegal evidence collection, but the court has no doubt about the legality of the obtaining of the defendant's pre-trial confession;
(3) The evidence provided by the public prosecutor is reliable and sufficient to exclude the possibility that the defendant's pre-trial confession was obtained illegally.
For the defendant's pre-trial confession read out in court, it shall be determined whether it may be used as the basis for adjudication in conjunction with the defendant's in-court confession and other evidence.
